          "type": "singleCorrect",
          "level": 1,
          "question": {
            "text": "A mixture of 2 moles of helium gas (atomic mass $=4 \\mathrm{amu}$ ) and 1 mole of argon gas (atomic mass $=40 \\mathrm{amu}$ ) is kept at $300 \\mathrm{~K}$ in a container. The ratio of the rms speeds $\\left(\\frac{v_{\\mathrm{rms}}(\\text { helium })}{v_{\\mathrm{rms}}(\\operatorname{argon})}\\right)$ is",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "477dk",
              "text": "$0.32$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "KpeMj",
              "text": "$0.45$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "FuyBk",
              "text": "$2.24$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "jOxLO",
              "text": "$3.16$",
              "isCorrect": true,
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "Using $V_{\\mathrm{rms}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{3 R T}{M}} \\Rightarrow V_{r m s} \\propto \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{M}}$ $\\frac{v_{\\text {rms (helium) }}}{v_{\\text {rms (argon) }}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{M_{\\text {argon }}}{M_{\\text {helium }}}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{40}{4}}=\\sqrt{10} \\approx 3.16$",
            "image": null
          },
          "videoSolution": null,
